B7845ab04\"><img src=\"https://link.axios.com/img/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94asj1el.94zk/10fc5fd7.gif\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\" /></a></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding-right:3.5%\" align=\"right\"> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47917533.426368/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2F4aW9zLWZpbmlzaC1saW5lLTQ4YjI1MjkwLTZhYWMtNDhkMS1iNDk2LWE5OTc2M2IwOWUyNC5odG1sP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBa4a6fde1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"b\" style=\"color:#222;font-size:13px;font-family:'gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;text-decoration:underline\">View in browser</a> </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"30\" style=\"height:30px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>  <tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1.3\"> </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"16\" style=\"height:16px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1\">\r\n<span class=\"s\" style=\"font-size:44px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#008dc8;letter-spacing:-1px;line-height:1\"> Axios Finish Line </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1.5;padding-bottom:35px;padding-top:10px\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#222;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">By  Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei  <span style=\"margin:0 6px\">&middot;</span> Oct 13, 2026 </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;line-height:1.75;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;padding:0 3.5%\"><p><strong>Welcome back! </strong>Axios national energy correspondent Amy Harder is guest-hosting tonight, reflecting on lessons from loss.</p><ul><li><em>Smart Brevity™count: 584 words … 2 mins. Copy edited by Amy Stern.</em></li></ul></td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing: Trying to bottle up life and its lessons </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td> <img src=\"https://images.axios.com/L_u-jCELNzqaIiGmGaI9EC4ifCk=/0x0:1920x1080/1920x1080/2026/10/13/1791920435301.jpeg\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item02\" alt=\"Illustration of a small glass bottle with a too-large note being stuffed in it. \"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Stock: Getty Images</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><em>Amy Harder writes:</em></p><p><strong>Death has a way </strong>of teaching us about living — if only life wouldn't get in the way.</p><ul><li><strong>Why it matters: </strong>Losing someone can bring sudden clarity to what actually matters. But making that change in perspective stick is hard.</li></ul><p><strong>My mother-in-law</strong> recently passed away, and almost immediately I<strong> </strong>wanted to bottle up everything our relationship and her death taught me.</p><ul><li><strong>These lessons</strong> — like making time for what matters, saying how you feel while you have the chance<strong> </strong>and taking more videos —<strong> </strong>are so obvious that they're easy to ignore until death makes them impossible to.</li></ul><p><strong>👓 The big picture: </strong>Death brings the fragility of life into sharp focus.</p><ul><li><strong>I suddenly wanted</strong> to hug everyone in my family as tightly as possible and somehow make all of us understand, right now, that we need to ensure we're making the most of our time together.</li></ul><p><strong>Reality check: </strong>Intellectually understanding that life is finite doesn't mean we can permanently feel the urgency of that fact. Yes, there's a temporary bump in togetherness, but then something maddening happens: Life goes on.</p><ul><li><strong>Jobs consume</strong> most of our waking hours during the week.</li><li><strong>Trips and other </strong>life obligations compete for our time.</li><li><strong>Sometimes we're</strong> simply tired and want to watch dumb TV shows.</li><li><strong>The profound realization</strong> that life is short somehow has to coexist with needing to unload the dishwasher.</li></ul><p><strong>💡 What I'm learning: </strong>Maybe I can't bottle up that feeling of urgency forever. But I don't have to preserve it at full strength for the experience to change me.</p><ul><li><strong>I want more videos</strong> and audio recordings<strong> </strong>of the people I love, particularly parents who may come second or third on the camera roll after children and pets. I recently asked my mother to leave me a happy birthday voice message. Now I'll have it forever.</li><li><strong>I want to keep </strong>showing up for the big moments while appreciating more of the utterly unremarkable ones: a grocery store trip, a random lunch, a phone conversation about nothing.</li></ul><p><strong>⏳ Yes, but: </strong>I want to be kinder to myself about the moments I will inevitably miss.</p><ul><li><strong>I've caught myself</strong> regretting time I didn't spend with loved ones, but I can't possibly be everywhere or do everything. The moments I miss don't diminish the ones I can make time for.</li></ul><p><strong>The bottom line</strong>: Death reminds us to live to the fullest. Life reminds us we can't always do that.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47917533.426368/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjYvMTAvMTQvbGlmZS1kZWF0aC1sZXNzb25zLWZpbmlzaC1saW5lP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB702c54a5\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Share this column</em></a><em>.</em></li></ul></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47917533.426368/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtNDhiMjUyOTAtNmFhYy00OGQxLWI0OTYtYTk5NzYzYjA5ZTI0Lmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QxJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkxJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB891d94ee\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47917533.426368/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-x-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Tweet this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47917533.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-linkedin-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Post to LinkedIn\"></a>  <a href=\"mailto:?subject=From Axios: 1 big thing: Trying to bottle up life and its lessons&body=teruyuki%40hh.iij4u.or.jp%20has%20shared%20an%20Axios%20story%20with%20you%3A%0A%0A1 big thing: Trying to bottle up life and its lessons%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2Fnewsletters%2Faxios-finish-line-48b25290-6aac-48d1-b496-a99763b09e24.html%3Fchunk%3D1%26utm_term%3Demshare%23story1\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-email-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Email this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47917533.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-sms-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Text this Story\"></a></td></tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      \r\n<tr><td height=\"20\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=\"ol-adpad\" style=\"padding: 20px 3.5% 0 3.5%;\"><p class=\"b\"\r\nstyle=\"-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100% !important; margin-bottom: 0 !important; font-size: 11px !important; letter-spacing: 1.4px; color: #008dc8; font-weight:700;\"\r\n>\r\nA MESSAGE FROM AXIOS\r\n</p></td></tr>\r\n<tr><td style=\"padding: 20px 3.5%; line-height: 1.5;\"><span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size: 26px; color: #222222;  font-family: 'gorditamedium', Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;  letter-spacing: -0.1px; line-height: 1.5;\">Find where your team is misaligned</span></td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"10\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td>\r\n<a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47917533.426368/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc21hcnRicmV2aXR5LmNvbS9zaW1wbGlmeS10cmFpbmluZz91dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249c2ltcGxpZnktd29ya3Nob3AmdXRtX3NvdXJjZT1heGlvcy1maW5pc2gtbGluZSZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXItYWQmdXRtX2NvbnRlbnQ9d29ya3Nob3AtYm9vayZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBfcba379b\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://images.axios.com/Frtiwe0Ep1vvM7X9iDHdzEyFu6I=/2026/10/08/1791490360635.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" /></a>\r\n</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"15\" style=\"height: 15px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td class=\"v\" style=\"padding: 0 3.5%; line-height: 1.75;  font-size: 17px; font-family: Georgia, serif; line-height: 1.75; color: #222222; letter-spacing: -0.1px;\">\r\n<p><strong>Simplify Workshop</strong> shows your team where it is misaligned and why it keeps happening.</p><p>Everyone leaves with one aligned set of priorities and a real kill list, built on the Confront, Delete, Amplify method. The whole team works through it together.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47917533.426368/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc21hcnRicmV2aXR5LmNvbS9zaW1wbGlmeS10cmFpbmluZz91dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249c2ltcGxpZnktd29ya3Nob3AmdXRtX3NvdXJjZT1heGlvcy1maW5pc2gtbGluZSZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXItYWQmdXRtX2NvbnRlbnQ9d29ya3Nob3AtYm9vayZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aCfcba379b\" target=\"_blank\">Learn more about the Workshop</a></strong></p>\r\n</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"10\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0; border-bottom: 10px solid #f5f5f5;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  2. 🍸 Lunch on me! </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td> <img src=\"https://images.axios.com/ud8rfh40ueCZbkwVGJxURHnu65E=/1920x1080/smart/2022/04/04/185030-1649098230583.jpg\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item03\" alt=\"Illustration of repeating dinner plate emojis with smiley faces on them.\"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Illustration: Maura Losch/Axios</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><strong>We love reading </strong>about the random acts of kindness Finish Line readers are encountering across the country. Here's one from Jan Lincoln of Mesa, Ariz.:</p><ul><li><strong>\"While my husband and I</strong> were waiting at an outdoor table at a cafe in Stanley, Idaho, I noticed a woman next to me reading and lunching alone. I wanted to know what she was reading, so I went to ask her. Turns out she was a bartender, and I'm a hobbyist mixologist.\"</li><li><strong>\"We talked cocktails </strong>for a bit until my order arrived. My husband and I enjoyed our lunch. Our neighbor departed with a nod and a wave. When we went to pay, we found out she'd paid for our lunch.\"</li></ul><p><strong>We'll keep featuring </strong>these nuggets of good news through the holiday season and beyond! Hit us at <a href=\"mailto:finishline@axios.com\" target=\"_blank\">finishline@axios.com</a> with your random act of kindness, plus your name and hometown.</p></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47917533.426368/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtNDhiMjUyOTAtNmFhYy00OGQxLWI0OTYtYTk5NzYzYjA5ZTI0Lmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QyJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkyJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aC6a34c822\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.a